e_region": {"id": 8, "region": "worldwide"}}, {"id": 854277, "date": 1748822400, "platform": 3, "y": 2025, "release_region": {"id": 8, "region": "worldwide"}}], "screenshots": [{"id": 1730422, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc1137a.jpg"}, {"id": 1730423, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc1137b.jpg"}, {"id": 1730424, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc1137c.jpg"}, {"id": 1730425, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc1137d.jpg"}, {"id": 1730426, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc1137e.jpg"}, {"id": 1730427, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc1137f.jpg"}, {"id": 1730428, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc1137g.jpg"}, {"id": 1730432, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc1137k.jpg"}, {"id": 1730433, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc1137l.jpg"}, {"id": 1730434, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc1137m.jpg"}, {"id": 1730435, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc1137n.jpg"}, {"id": 1730436, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc1137o.jpg"}, {"id": 1730437, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc1137p.jpg"}, {"id": 1730438, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc1137q.jpg"}, {"id": 1730439, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc1137r.jpg"}, {"id": 1730431, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc1137j.jpg"}, {"id": 1730429, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc1137h.jpg"}, {"id": 1730430, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc1137i.jpg"}], "slug": "cross-the-world", "storyline": "\"I guess it's another open-world survival craft RPG, how is it different this time?\"\nEver thought of an open-world game where stuff in the background never disappears into thin air, or map chunks don\u2019t freeze with everything in them\u2014NPCs, trees, animals, etc.\u2014until the player walks nearby?\n\nHow about an open world where nature and the environment constantly progress with the flow of time into the future, with weather, temperature, and seasons shaping the world as they go, and whatever changes you or the world have made are persistent throughout the entirety of the game world?\n\nFor example, the fruits you harvested from a tree would rot and eventually disappear even after you\u2019ve moved away from the area, and the trees would change shape with the seasons and bear fruit again the following year.\n\nCross The World started as a very ambitious project, an answer to that itch I\u2019ve always felt as a gamer who wanted a game just like that.", "summary": "Explore, gather, craft, fight, and survive the fantasy world with persistent world simulation as an adventurer party. Every part of the world is persistently calculated, environment interacts and changes over time with season and progress. Play alone or play with your friends in multiplayer!", "themes": [{"id": 17, "name": "Fantasy"}, {"id": 21, "name": "Survival"}, {"id": 33, "name": "Sandbox"}, {"id": 38, "name": "Open world"}], "url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/cross-the-world", "videos": [{"id": 172331, "name": "Trailer", "video_id": "LFsBwyxGIgA", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LFsBwyxGIgA", "title": "Cross The World - Early Access Trailer", "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/LFsBwyxGIgA/maxresdefault.jpg"}]}